istorical heading's exemption. Existing English and substantive-change checks remain enforced.\n\nRepair source commit: `cc15632d0d5f200d0660a8b41cd576efbdfab5a1` (tree `f8bc0d056d9c115e764402fe80779f2383b97353`). The baseline witness exposed four missed claims; focused coverage and 40 independently executed CLI cases validate the repair and adversarial boundaries. Source-fixed does not imply live verification or prove that arbitrary accompanying executable changes are relevant to a claim.\n\nThe reconciliation changes only `BRAIN-TRANSITION-GUARD-BLIND-TO-ARABIC-STATUS-01` from open to fixed. Current totals are 526 IDs: 134 open, 389 fixed, 3 verified. The included 135-open-gap plan is explicitly the historical `9a50aac3bf71ed42f4fad91a036d49e61d151a52` baseline, with 35 bounded next actions and 100 decision/operator/external dependencies; those actions are not promises of complete code-only closure. CDSE remains open while its actual PR #1182 merge, final-head CI, and deployment receipts are appended without rewriting earlier evidence.\n\nThe full source validation below ran with HEAD at the real repair commit above and staged index/working files at opening tree `36fa76cae2768bf08f94e0fc046ea29f94092482`. The PR #1183 provenance cycle then changed only evidence, brain appendices and generated outputs, producing final API commit `0126ae7894b18cd4f3e3ebcc1afcc7dd19392374` and exact tree `6a297aae1272217b9e73e055312d7554f851568c`; source and test hashes remain identical:\n\n- Full native preflight with generation and convergence completed exit 0, with zero failures and two explicit security-tool PATH skips. Both skipped gates subsequently completed exit 0 using the existing security environment: high-severity Bandit and the exact native pip-audit command. The workflow's separate 19-requirements pip-audit command also completed exit 0 with its existing exceptions unchanged.\n- Normal and C-locale unit suites each passed 8,878 tests with 39 skips; repository tests passed 996 with 8 skips; platform tests passed 4,586; all 169 guards survived C locale.\n- The path-only change guard, heading/state guard, numerical registry-claim guard, frozen-path guard, certification evidence-producer guard, and final probe-leak guard passed. Opening release packaging validated 6,315 checksums. The final provenance cycle passed 142 relevant metadata/brain tests and five standalone guards, full generated-artifact repair and convergence, then release packaging last with 6,321 checksums. An interrupted convergence attempt had no exit receipt; its successful measured replacement is recorded separately, without inferring success for the interrupted attempt.\n- All three actual committed-range guards passed for `9a50aac3bf71ed42f4fad91a036d49e61d151a52..0126ae7894b18cd4f3e3ebcc1afcc7dd19392374`: brain state transitions, commit claims, and append-only history. The final API commit exactly matches tested final tree `6a297aae1272217b9e73e055312d7554f851568c`. Capability impact was freshly derived from this actual committed range and merged base/head evidence mappings, and the live PR body declaration is checked against it. Final-head GitHub CI remains pending; no JUnit output or successful final-head remote run is claimed by these local receipts.\n\nThe exact final 50-path committed range has zero matches against 60 Railway watch patterns across 43 live configurations refreshed at 2026-10-14 16:31:40–16:31:42 UTC; all staged configurations were null and there was no frozen service-path intersection. This is a configuration-based impact estimate; actual post-merge deployments remain a separate check. No database, secret, service configuration, or live-provider mutation is included. Compact full-gate receipts, command/log hashes, the real PR #1183 reference, and opening API identity/range/body evidence were tracked before final provenance generation and packaging. Fresh final-commit range and body gates are now measured; final-head remote CI and actual deployment review remain separate gates.\n\nCapability-Impact: FM-007, INT-004, IRR-003, IRR-009, SAT-001, SEC-003\n","created_at":"2026-10-14T15:59:41Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T17:11:24Z","closed_at":"2026-10-14T17:11:22Z","merged_at":"2026-10-14T17:11:21Z","merge_commit_sha":"56de3d316fd5243253b6f6d38dc38b331bbddf95","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kafaat/ai_platform_complete_v2.0.0_enhanced/pulls/1183/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kafaat/ai_platform_complete_v2.0.0_enhanced/pulls/1183/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kafaat/ai_platform_complete_v2.0.0_enhanced/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kafaat/ai_platform_complete_v2.0.0_enhanced/issues/1183/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kafaat/ai_platform_complete_v2.0.0_enhanced/statuses/0126ae7894b18cd4f3e3ebcc1afcc7dd19392374","head":{"label":"kafaat:codex/arabic-state-guard-20261014","ref":"codex/arabic-state-guard-20261014","sha":"0126ae7894b18cd4f3e3ebcc1afcc7dd19392374","user":{"login":"kafaat","id":80758750,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwNzU4NzUw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/80758750?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kafaat","html_url":"https://github.com/kafaat","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kafaat/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kafaat/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kafaat/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kafaat/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kafaat/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kafaat/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kafaat/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kafaat/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/k